Here we model the cumulative change but account for the accumulated error in the cumulative sum. We treat the residual process within each plot × trait as a Wiener process started at the initial census \(t0\). The covariance between any two observations i, j from the same plot × trait is then: \(Cov(resid_i, resid_j) = \sigma^2\cdot(min(t_i, t_j) − t0)\). We replace the independent-normal likelihood with a multivariate normal (via Cholesky decomposition) over each plot x trait block.


